abstract: >
  Information-set conditional, fail-closed auditing framework for quantum and
  classical collider event classifiers under experimental systematic
  uncertainties and quantum estimation uncertainty: anytime-valid
  certification (exact weighted extension), formal identifiability results,
  partial-label certification landscapes, physics-level inference validation,
  and a CMS Open Data + IBM Quantum hardware deployment ledger.
keywords:
  - quantum machine learning
  - distribution shift
  - anytime-valid inference
  - collider physics
  - certification
